 "grammar": {
  "title": {
   "ko": "구동사 check in / take off / get on / get off",
   "en": "travel phrasal verbs: check in, take off, get on, get off"
  },
  "explain": {
   "ko": "여행에서는 check in / check out(호텔·공항), take off(이륙하다), get on / get off(버스·기차·비행기에 타다 / 내리다), set off(출발하다), pick up(마중하다) 같은 구동사를 자주 씁니다. 택시·승용차는 get in / get out of를 씁니다.",
   "en": "On trips you often use check in / check out (hotels and airports), take off (planes), get on / get off (buses, trains, planes), set off (start a journey) and pick up (meet someone). For cars and taxis use get in / get out of."
  },
  "table": {
   "head": [
    "표현 / Pattern",
    "예 / Example"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "check in / out",
     "We checked in at the hotel."
    ],
    [
     "take off",
     "The plane takes off at eight."
    ],
    [
     "get on / off",
     "I got on the bus. Get off at the next station."
    ],
    [
     "set off / pick up",
     "We set off early. I picked up my friend."
    ]
   ]
  },
  "notes": [
   {
    "ko": "버스·기차·비행기는 get on / get off, 택시·자동차는 get in / get out of.",
    "en": "get on / off for buses, trains and planes; get in / out of for cars and taxis."
   },
   {
    "ko": "check in은 도착 때, check out은 떠날 때.",
    "en": "check in on arrival, check out on leaving."
   },
   {
    "ko": "set off는 여행을 시작하다.",
    "en": "set off means to start a journey."
   }
  ],
  "examples": [
